  "question": {
    "text": "The lock of a safe consists of five discs each of which features the digits <math> <mrow> <mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>....</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9.</mn></mrow> </math> The safe can be opened by dialing a special combination of the digits. If the work day lasts <math> <mrow> <mn>13</mn></mrow> </math> hours and to dial&nbsp;one combination of digits takes <math> <mn>5</mn> </math> seconds, then&nbsp;number of days sufficient enough to open the safe, are",
